  "new_term_search": "Sodium Tungstate Dihydrate (https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/150191)\nciteturn48search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; # Sodium Tungstate Dihydrate ... URL: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?\n\n### Other Identifiers\n\nChEBI ID\n    CHEBI:63939\n\n### Compound Titles\n\n  * Sodium Tungstate Dihydrate\n\n### IUPAC Names\n\n  * disodium;dioxido(dioxo)tungsten;dihydrate\n\n### Third-Party Identifiers\n\nIdentifier  | Identifier Type\n--- | ---\n10213-10-2  | CAS\nCHEBI:63939  | ChEBI ID\nDTXSID0032079  | DSSTox Substance ID\n600-275-2  | European Community (EC) Number\nX1F4NY6U13  | UNII\nQ27132921  | Wikidata\n\n### Synonyms\n\n#### MeSH Entry Terms\n\n  * sodium tungstate(VI) dihydrate\n  * sodium tungstate dihydrate\n\nSource: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH); Context: Medical Subject Heading (MeSH) names or identifiers matching this PubChem Compound record. The matching between the MeSH and compound records is performed by name matching (i.e., identical common names), as described in Kim et al., J. Cheminform., 2016, 8, 32.; Section reference: http://doi.org/10.1186/s13321-016-0142-6\n\n#### Depositor-Supplied Synonyms\n\n  * Sodium tungstate dihydrate\n  * 10213-10-2\nSome large, complex, or highly symmetric structures may fail this process.\n\n## Selected PubChem Annotations\n\n### Record Description\n\nSodium tungstate dihydrate is a hydrate that is the dihydrate form of sodium tungstate. Combines with hydrogen peroxide for the oxidation of secondary amines to nitrones. It has a role as a reagent. It contains a sodium tungstate.\n\nURL: https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/Sodium%20tungstate%20dihydrate\n\nURL: https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/sodium%20tungstate\n\nURL: https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/hydrogen%20peroxide\n\nURL: https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/sodium%20tungstate\n\nValue name: Record Description\n\nValue qualifier: Ontology Summary\n\n#### Source\n\nSource: ChEBI\n\nSource ID: CHEBI:OBO:150191\n\nSource record name: Sodium tungstate dihydrate\n\nSource description: Chemical Entities of Biological Interest (ChEBI) is a database and ontology of molecular entities focused on 'small' chemical compounds, that is part of the Open Biomedical Ontologies effort. The term \"molecular entity\" refers to any constitutionally or isotopically distinct atom, molecule, ion, ion pair, radical, radical ion, complex, conformer, etc., identifiable as a separately distinguishable entity.\n\nURL: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:63939\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAmiGO 2: Term Details for \"monosodium glutamate\" (CHEBI:64220) (https://amigo.geneontology.org/amigo/term/CHEBI%3A64220)\nciteturn48search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; ##### Parents of monosodium glutamate (CHEBI:64220)\n\nThe term CHEBI:64220 is not an internal term, but likely comes from an external resource. For full information on this term, please refer to the originating resource.\n\n# monosodium glutamate\n\n### Term Information\n\nFeedback \n\nAccession\n    CHEBI:64220\nName\n    monosodium glutamate\nOntology\n    chebi_ontology\nSynonyms\n    sodium 2-azaniumylpentanedioate, MSG, sodium 2-ammoniopentanedioate, sodium 2-azaniumylpentanedioate, sodium glutamate\nAlternate IDs\n    None\nDefinition\n    An organic sodium salt that is the monosodium salt of glutamic acid. [source: unknown]\nComment\n    None\nChem. react.\n    None\nSubset\n    3:STAR\n\n##### Parents of monosodium glutamate (CHEBI:64220)\n\nsubjectImage: Reorder by subject  | relationImage: Reorder by relation  | objectImage: Reorder by object\n--- | --- | ---\nmonosodium glutamate  | Image: is_a relation is_a   | organic sodium salt (CHEBI:38700)\nmonosodium glutamate  | Image: BFO:0000051 relation BFO:0000051   | glutamate(1-) (CHEBI:14321)\n\n##### Children of monosodium glutamate (CHEBI:64220)\n\nsubjectImage: Reorder by subjec