ral W is double-bonded to O above and connected to O⁻ groups below and to the right; Na⁺ is shown beside the right-hand O⁻ and Na⁺ below the lower O⁻.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nATSDR Tungsten Tox Profile (https://www.atsdr.cdc.gov/toxprofiles/tp186.pdf)\nciteturn48search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 21.3 years ago; Crawled: 15.0 years ago; <td>Disodium tetraoxatungstate (2-), dihydrate; tetraoxo-tungstate (2-); disodium tungstate, dihydrate; sodium tungsten oxide, dihydrate; sodium wolframate, dihydrate; tungstic acid, disodium salt, dihydrate</td>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSafety data sheet Safety Data Sheet (https://www.carlroth.com/medias/SDB-3666-GB-EN.pdf?context=bWFzdGVyfHNlY3VyaXR5RGF0YXNoZWV0c3wyNDQ0MzJ8YXBwbGljYXRpb24vcGRmfGFHRXhMMmd6Tmk4NU1qTXpOREkyT1RNNU9UTTBMMU5FUWw4ek5qWTJYMGRDWDBWT0xuQmtaZ3w1OTBmODRkMGRjNTA0MjY1NDY5NDZhNjYwNDA1MDhlODI2NjI3OWU3ZTU5ZDcwNWMwZjdmMTYxMWI3NmVjMmNh)\nciteturn48search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Ammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate ≥99 %, p.a.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAmmonium orthomolybdate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ammonium_orthomolybdate)\nciteturn48search18 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Upon heating these solutions, ammonia is lost, to give ammonium heptamolybdate ((NH_{4})_{6}Mo_{7}O_{24}·4H_{2}O). ... Heating ammonium orthomolybdate solid or treatment with acid gives molybdenum trioxide.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAmmonium heptamolybdate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ammonium_heptamolybdate)\nciteturn48search19 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 9 months ago; Ammonium heptamolybdate is the inorganic compound whose chemical formula is (NH_{4})_{6}Mo_{7}O_{24}, normally encountered as the tetrahydrate. ... Ammonium heptamolybdate is easily prepared by dissolving molybdenum trioxide in an excess of aqueous ammonia and evaporating the solution at room temperature.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSodium tungstate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_tungstate)\nciteturn48search20 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Sodium tungstate can also be produced by treating tungsten carbide with a mixture of sodium nitrate and sodium hydroxide in a fusion process which overcomes the high exothermicity of the reaction involved. ... As such, one niche use of sodium tungstate is in experimental biology—where it has been found that adding sodium tungstate to the drinking water of mice inhibits the growth of Enterobacteriaceae (a family of endogenous opportunistic pathogens) in the gut.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMonosodium glutamate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monosodium_glutamate)\nciteturn48search21 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Monosodium glutamate (MSG), also known as sodium glutamate, is a sodium salt of glutamic acid. ... Ikeda called his product \"monosodium glutamate\" and submitted a patent to produce MSG; the Suzuki brothers began commercial production of MSG in 1909 using the term Ajinomoto (\"essence of taste\").\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAmmonium molybdate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ammonium_molybdate)\nciteturn48search22 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4.5 years ago; * Ammonium heptamolybdate, (NH_{4})_{6}Mo_{7}O_{24}, usually encountered as the tetrahydrate\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nE number (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E_number)\nciteturn48search23 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;  E621  | Monosodium glutamate (MSG)  | flavour enhancer  | Approved in the EU.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDissolving ammonium molybdate heptahydrate in water (https://www.reddit.com/r/chemistry/comments/12259ah)\nciteturn48reddit24 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.6 years ago; The problem was NOT the new brand of the reagent, what finally worked was adjusting the pH of the water to 7-8 first using NaOH pellets, and then adding the ammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAmmonium molybdate questions (https://www.reddit.com/r/chemistry/comments/1e1l26k)\nciteturn48reddit25 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Crawled: 2.3 years ago; Hi all, I came across a paper that uses ammonium heptamolybdate as a catalyst in hydrogen peroxide analysis. ... Yes, this makes an ammonia/ammonium buffer to control the speciation of the polyoxo(peroxo)molybdates.\n",
